# Petpooja POSS reverse engineering

When the user asks to build or match a feature the same way as Petpooja POSS, read the local checkout of https://github.com/morluto/rea at `rea/` before implementing. Use its captured routes, session notes, JavaScript route inventory, and agent-environment specs to see how that screen behaves. Product notes stay in `docs/petpooja-billing/` and `docs/petpooja-clone/`.

- Checkout path: `rea/` (a local clone of `https://github.com/morluto/rea`).
- Do not `git add` `rea/`, do not commit it, and do not remove `rea/` from `.gitignore`.
- Source Control hides this nested checkout with `git.ignoredRepositories` in `.vscode/settings.json`. Leave that setting in place.
- If `rea/` is missing, restore it with `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/morluto/rea.git rea` and leave it untracked.
